",\n  \"src_claim_id\": \"claim-agreement-among-full-patch-elided-and-predicted-fidelities-on-classically-verifi--c34d4d1d9279\",\n  \"src_claim_ref\": \"7\",\n  \"status\": \"open\"\n}\n/Users/chrgre01/src/Sapi/verification/example_site/spaces/quantum-physics/relations/rel-9a0c58940fa79b4ac7c8bb90346d9fe305b805b3dd6f4d294439ac631e405898.json\n--- /Users/chrgre01/src/Sapi/verification/example_site/spaces/quantum-physics/relations/rel-9a0c58940fa79b4ac7c8bb90346d9fe305b805b3dd6f4d294439ac631e405898.json ---\n{\n  \"below_040_streak\": 0,\n  \"contradiction_confidence_band\": \"unknown\",\n  \"dst_claim_id\": \"claim-for-the-hardest-reported-random-circuit-sampling-task-sycamore-produced-one-mill--07db9778c4a3\",\n  \"dst_claim_ref\": \"1\",\n  \"last_evaluated_run_id\": null,\n  \"rationale\": \"The measured elided-circuit fidelity is needed for the equal-fidelity runtime comparison behind the speedup claim.\",\n  \"relation_file_id\": \"rel-9a0c58940fa79b4ac7c8bb90346d9fe305b805b3dd6f4d294439ac631e405898\",\n  \"relation_id\": \"supports:claim-the-largest-elided-53-qubit-20-cycle-circuits-yielded-f-xeb-2-24-0-21-10-3-over--0a24f12d0686->claim-for-the-hardest-reported-random-circuit-sampling-task-sycamore-produced-one-mill--07db9778c4a3\",\n  \"relation_type\": \"supports\",\n  \"src_claim_id\": \"claim-the-largest-elided-53-qubit-20-cycle-circuits-yielded-f-xeb-2-24-0-21-10-3-over--0a24f12d0686\",\n  \"src_claim_ref\": \"3\",\n  \"status\": \"open\"\n}\n/Users/chrgre01/src/Sapi/verification/example_site/spaces/quantum-physics/relations/rel-4ac498834bf6ba48fe220c06cf1193f880e33a9aaf768679fd7bec48aa6917e1.json\n--- /Users/chrgre01/src/Sapi/verification/example_site/spaces/quantum-physics/relations/rel-4ac498834bf6ba48fe220c06cf1193f880e33a9aaf768679fd7bec48aa6917e1.json ---\n{\n  \"below_040_streak\": 0,\n  \"contradiction_confidence_band\": \"unknown\",\n  \"dst_claim_id\": \"claim-nisq-devices-are-best-understood-as-experimental-tools-for-exploring-many-body-q--fde7f9646dbb\",\n  \"dst_claim_ref\": \"1\",\n  \"last_evaluated_run_id\": null,\n  \"rationale\": \"The overhead and distance of fault tolerance support the claim that NISQ is a stepping stone rather than an immediate transformation.\",\n  \"relation_file_id\": \"rel-4ac498834bf6ba48fe220c06cf1193f880e33a9aaf768679fd7bec48aa6917e1\",\n  \"relation_id\": \"supports:claim-scalable-fault-tolerant-quantum-computing-depends-on-quantum-error-correction-bu--cf48bc246343->claim-nisq-devices-are-best-understood-as-experimental-tools-for-exploring-many-body-q--fde7f9646dbb\",\n  \"relation_type\": \"supports\",\n  \"src_claim_id\": \"claim-scalable-fault-tolerant-quantum-computing-depends-on-quantum-error-correction-bu--cf48bc246343\",\n  \"src_claim_ref\": \"3\",\n  \"status\": \"open\"\n}\n--- source headings ---\n102:                       A QUANTUM INTERFACE BETWEEN LIGHT AND MATTER\n141:                                  CAVITY QUANTUM ELECTRODYNAMICS\n295:                           QUANTUM NETWORKS WITH ATOMIC ENSEMBLES\n313:          L       R\n415:                       EXTENDING ENTANGLEMENT FOR QUANTUM NETWORKS\n447:                                                    CONCLUSION\n667:IARPA, and by Northrop Grumman Space Technology.\n674:               BOX 1 - MAPPING QUANTUM STATES BETWEEN ATOMS AND PHOTONS\n711:                               BOX 2 - A NEW PARADIGM FOR CAVITY QED\n748:                   BOX 3 - WRITING AND READING SINGLE ATOMIC EXCITATIONS\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
