remote quantum memories [92]. The experiment shown in Fig. 3(c) [93] took an important step towards this goal\n388-by achieving the minimal functionality required for scalable quantum networks. Heralded entanglement was created\n--\n450-insights and experimental capabilities in the quest to realize functional quantum networks. Certainly, the current state\n451-of the art is primitive relative to that required for the robust and scalable implementation of sophisticated network\n452-protocols, whether over short or long distances. The realization of quantum memories, local quantum processing,\n453:quantum repeaters, and error-corrected teleportation are very ambitious goals. There is nevertheless considerable\n454-activity worldwide directed towards these important goals.\n455-   While my discussion has considered separately cavity QED-based networks and those implemented via the DLCZ\n456-protocol, clearly quantum networks will evolve as heterogeneous entities. For example, the same protocol that creates\n--\n616-      ensembles. Phys. Rev. A 76, 012301 (2007).\n617- [78] Zhao, B., Chen, Z. -B., Chen, Y. -A., Schmiedmayer, J & Pan, J. -W. Robust creation of entanglement between remote\n618-      memory qubits. Phys. Rev. Lett. 98, 240502 (2007).\n619: [79] Sangouard, N. et al., Robust and efficient quantum repeaters with atomic ensembles and linear optics, available at\n620-      http://arxiv.org/abs/0802.1475.\n621- [80] Harris, S. E. Electromagnetically induced transparency. Phys. Today 50, 36-40 (1997).\n622- [81] Kuzmich, A., Bowen, W. P., Boozer, A. D., Boca, A., Chou, C. W., Duan, L. -M. & Kimble, H. J. Generation of\n\n--- pattern: functional quantum nodes ---\n348-3). b) Experimentally determined elements of the density matrix ρexp   L,R for entanglement between two atomic ensembles [75],\n349-corresponding to concurrence C = 0.9 ± 0.3, where C = 0 for an unentangled state. For comparison the density matrix ρth  L,R for\n350-the ideal state |ΨL,R i is shown with concurrence C = 1. c) Photograph of the laboratory setup for entanglement of two pairs\n351:of atomic ensembles for the realization of functional quantum nodes L, R separated by 3 m [93]. The four˛ elongated\n352-                                                                                                             ¸ ˛      ovals each\n353-show a cylinder of 105 Cesium atoms which forms an atomic ensemble at each site. Entangled states ˛ΨuL,R , ˛ΨlL,R between\n354-                                                                                                                      ¸\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
