surement-error-rates-imply-that-uncorrected-nisq-c--68f47af68b82\\\",\n        \\\"claim-quantum-computers-have-credible-grounds-for-super-classical-power-because-of-kno--2f85bd581bbb\\\",\n        \\\"claim-random-quantum-circuits-become-exponentially-harder-to-simulate-classically-as-q--f7cd81f80f31\\\",\n        \\\"claim-linear-cross-entropy-benchmarking-provides-a-fidelity-measure-by-comparing-exper--4abac38b173d\\\",\n        \\\"claim-agreement-among-full-patch-elided-and-predicted-fidelities-on-classically-verifi--c34d4d1d9279\\\",\n        \\\"claim-for-the-hardest-reported-random-circuit-sampling-task-sycamore-produced-one-mill--07db9778c4a3\\\",\n        \\\"claim-the-demonstrated-speedup-is-specific-to-random-circuit-sampling-and-does-not-rem--47d4f349751e\\\",\n        \\\"claim-quantum-connectivity-gives-linked-nodes-a-state-space-that-scales-exponentially--50cc8b700a70\\\",\n        \\\"claim-full-density-matrix-characterization-becomes-an-impractical-verification-strateg--65a0be3566e1\\\"\n      ],\n      \\\"source_ids\\\": [\n        \\\"source-01-quantum-computing-in-the-nisq-era-and-beyond--2ce59b8ba8bb\\\",\n        \\\"source-02-quantum-supremacy-using-a-programmable-superconducting-processor--f98990eb22d8\\\",\n        \\\"source-03-the-quantum-internet--cd7f6b2f11e2\\\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"topic_id\\\": \\\"topic-coherent-interfaces-for-scaling-quantum-systems\\\",\n      \\\"title\\\": \\\"Coherent interfaces for scaling quantum systems\\\",\n      \\\"structure_type\\\": \\\"wiki\\\",\n      \\\"sections\\\": [\n        \\\"This topic synthesizes the hardware-facing requirement shared by quantum computing and quantum networking sources: useful scaling depends not only on more qubits, but on preserving coherence while operations, measurements, and interfaces become larger and more complex.\\\",\n        \\\"The NISQ and Sycamore sources quantify this pressure through gate and readout errors, circuit depth, predicted fidelity, and the importance of lowering two-qubit gate errors. The quantum-internet source describes the networking analogue: reversible light-matter interconnects, strong cavity-QED coupling, dark-state mappings, controlled cavity pulses, and EIT-based ensemble memories must move quantum states between stationary and flying systems without destroying entanglement.\\\",\n        \\\"A concept page can compare local processor scaling with network scaling: both need error-aware physical mechanisms, but networked systems add conversion between matter and light, heterogeneous nodes, and entanglement-preserving interfaces as first-class design constraints.\\\"\n      ],\n      \\\"claim_ids\\\": [\n        \\\"claim-lower-gate-error-rates-matter-both-because-they-allow-larger-uncorrected-nisq-ci--043e58605f51\\\",\n        \\\"claim-measured-component-error-rates-under-simultaneous-operation-were-low-enough-to-s--6d6ae35745de\\\",\n        \\\"claim-the-largest-random-circuits-combined-53-qubits-1-113-single-qubit-gates-430-two--c8ece98aae87\\\",\n        \\\"claim-large-quantum-networks-require-reversible-interconnects-that-convert-quantum-sta--03b0b3a11218\\\",\n        \\\"claim-strong-cavity-qed-coupling-supplies-a-physical-regime-in-which-individual-atoms--9807d4e35625\\\",\n        \\\"claim-dark-state-adiabatic-control-can-reversibly-map-a-single-photon-optical-field-in--55c6ef7fe1ba\\\",\n        \\\"claim-controlled-cavity-pulses-can-generate-entanglement-first-between-an-atom-and-an--ee045e1c7175\\\",\n        \\\"claim-electromagnetically-induced-transparency-enables-deterministic-reversible-mappin--b76e4e96d4f0\\\"\n      ],\n      \\\"source_ids\\\": [\n        \\\"source-01-quantum-computing-in-the-nisq-era-and-beyond--2ce59b8ba8bb\\\",\n        \\\"source-02-quantum-supremacy-using-a-programmable-superconducting-processor--f98990eb22d8\\\",\n        \\\"source-03-the-quantum-internet--cd7f6b2f11e2\\\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"topic_id\\\": \\\"topic-entanglement-as-resource-and-bottleneck\\\",\n      \\\"title\\\": \\\"Entanglement as both resource and bottleneck\\\",\n      \\\"structure_type\\\": \\\"wiki\\\",\n      \\\"sections\\\": [\n        \\\"This topic treats entanglement as the common resource behind quantum advantage claims, many-body NISQ exploration, random-circuit hardness, and quantum-network protocols, while also noting that entanglement makes control, verification, and scaling difficult.\\\",\n        \\\"Preskill identifies highly entangled quantum dynamics as a natural arena for meaningful quantum advantage and describes NISQ devices as tools for exploring many-body physics. Sycamore uses random circuits whose unstructured output distributions become exponentially harder to simulate as qubits and cycles grow. Kimble's quantum-internet discussion shifts from entanglement inside one processor to entanglement distributed across matter-light interfaces and atomic ensembles, including DLCZ heralding and stored ensemble entanglement.\\\",\n        \\\"The synthesis should avoid implying that all entanglement is equally useful: the evidence supports entanglement as necessary for hard quantum behavior and network connectivity, but also shows that practical value depends on fidelity, controllability, memory retrieval, and verification methods.\\\"\n      ],\n      \\\"claim_ids\\\": [\n        \\\"claim-highly-entangled-quantum-dynamics-is-the-most-natural-arena-for-meaningful-quant--3b6f2f5ba268\\\",\n        \\\"claim-nisq-devices-are-best-understood-as-experimental-tools-for-exploring-many-body-q--fde7f9646dbb\\\",\n        \\\"claim-random-quantum-circuits-become-exponentially-harder-to-simulate-classically-as-q--f7cd81f80f31\\\",\n        \\\"claim-the-sycamore-superconducting-processor-created-random-circuit-quantum-states-on--2b4eeabd4063\\\",\n        \\\"claim-the-dlcz-protocol-creates-heralded-entanglement-between-atomic-ensembles-by-inte--aa516185d3b2\\\",\n        \\\"claim-atomic-ensemble-experiments-had-achieved-stored-heralded-entanglement-high-retri--7d38956d9ede\\\",\n        \\\"claim-scalable-quantum-networks-are-likely-to-be-heterogeneous-systems-that-combine-ca--dfe53fef0772\\\"\n      ],\n      \\\"source_ids\\\": [\n        \\\"source-01-quantum-computing-in-the-nisq-era-and-beyond--2ce59b8ba8bb\\\",\n        \\\"source-02-quantum-supremacy-using-a-programmable-superconducting-processor--f98990eb22d8\\\",\n        \\\"source-03-the-quantum-internet--cd7f6b2f11e2\\\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"topic_id\\\": \\\"topic-near-term-demonstrations-versus-fault-tolerant-systems\\\",\n      \\\"title\\\": \\\"Near-term demonstrations versus fault-tolerant quantum systems\\\",\n      \\\"structure_type\\\": \\\"wiki\\\",\n      \\\"sections\\\": [\n        \\\"This topic compares demonstrated or plausible near-term quantum capabilities with the longer path to robust, scalable systems. It is supported across all three sources, but the strength of evidence differs by domain: Sycamore reports a concrete task-specific sampling demonstration, while NISQ algorithms and large quantum networks remain more conditional roadmaps.\\\",\n        \\\"The NISQ source distinguishes experimental value and heuristic testbeds from transformative fault-tolerant applications, emphasizing error-correction overhead and unresolved performance of QAOA/VQE against mature classical methods. The Sycamore source reports random-circuit sampling speedup but explicitly leaves Shor-style factoring and other applications dependent on fault-tolerant logical qubits. The quantum-internet source surveys primitive but real demonstrations while noting that repeaters, local processing, error-corrected teleportation, and scalable verification remain ambitious goals.\\\",\n        \\\"A page on this concept can help prevent overclaiming: near-term devices can be scientifically important and sometimes classically hard, yet the evidence does not support broad claims that they already deliver general-purpose, fault-tolerant quantum computing or fully scalable quantum networking.\\\"\n      ],\n      \\\"claim_ids\\\": [\n        \\\"claim-hybrid-qaoa-and-vqe-approaches-are-plausible-nisq-era-testbeds-but-their-ability--31ec67369767\\\",\n        \\\"claim-quantum-computers-are-not-expected-to-efficiently-solve-hard-np-hard-combinatori--0d5f718c4d47\\\",\n        \\\"claim-scalable-fault-tolerant-quantum-computing-depends-on-quantum-error-correction-bu--cf48bc246343\\\",\n        \\\"claim-noise-resilient-circuit-design-can-extend-nisq-computational-reach-but-it-may-tr--aed4bcfeaa39\\\",\n        \\\"claim-the-demonstrated-speedup-is-specific-to-random-circuit-sampling-and-does-not-rem--47d4f349751e\\\",\n        \\\"claim-the-largest-elided-53-qubit-20-cycle-circuits-yielded-f-xeb-2-24-0-21-10-3-over--0a24f12d0686\\\",\n        \\\"claim-scalable-quantum-networks-are-likely-to-be-heterogeneous-systems-that-combine-ca--dfe53fef0772\\\",\n        \\\"claim-atomic-ensemble-experiments-had-achieved-stored-heralded-entanglement-high-retri--7d38956d9ede\\\"\n      ],\n      \\\"source_ids\\\": [\n        \\\"source-01-quantum-computing-in-the-nisq-era-and-beyond--2ce59b8ba8bb\\\",\n        \\\"source-02-quantum-supremacy-using-a-programmable-superconducting-processor--f98990eb22d8\\\",\n        \\\"source-03-the-quantum-internet--cd7f6b2f11e2\\\"\n      ]\n    }\n  ]\n}\n\noutput_path.write_text(json.dumps(obj, ensure_ascii=False, indent=2) + '\\\\n', encoding='utf-8')\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
